    "description": "## Objective\n\nAdd duplicate prevention across the reference data objects so bad records are blocked or flagged at entry. Split out from the object-creation stories so those are not blocked by rule tuning.\n\n## Implementation Requirements\n\n* Operator: matching rule + duplicate rule blocking a second Operator with the same Name\n* Partner: matching rule + duplicate rule blocking a second Partner with the same Name\n* Deal: enforce uniqueness on the Partner + Operator + Market + Vertical + Version combination — composite external key field populated by flow with a unique constraint, or validation via duplicate rule; block or flag Review Required per design story C-01\n* Confirm rules do not interfere with the data loader (allow bypass for bulk migration where intended)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n* A duplicate Operator Name is blocked\n* A duplicate Partner Name is blocked\n* A second active Deal with the same Partner + Operator + Market + Vertical + Version is blocked or flagged Review Required\n* Sample data load (POC-11 pattern) still succeeds with rules active\n\n## Testing Notes\n\nAttempt duplicates on all three objects; re-run a small sample load with rules on.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nPerson Account (Player/Referrer) matching and duplicate rules — covered by BUILD-03.\n\n## Open Questions\n\n* For Deal duplicates: hard-block on save, or allow save + flag Review Required? Design doc permits either.\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n* Estimate is rough (\\~6–10h) pending the block-vs-flag decision; composite-key flow approach is the higher end.\n* Person-record dedupe (Player/Referrer email uniqueness, matching rules, cross-linking) stays in BUILD-03 as its own ticket.\n\n---\n\nEstimate: M · \\~8h (rough) · Dependencies: POC-03, POC-04, POC-06 · Ticket BUILD-08 (approved 2026-07-04)",
